# SABOTAGE: MG-21 (ADR-049 mutation ledger) — `Samen.Policy.SameOrgFk.target_org_id/2`'s
# repo resolution order is severed: `repo(dest, :read) || repo(dest)` becomes `&&`, so the
# READ repo is no longer tried first and no longer suffices. A destination whose repo
# resolves for `:read` and not for `:mutate` — AshPostgres's own documented function-repo
# shape, the read-replica split — then resolves to nil, the guard bails out
# `{:error, :no_data_layer}`, and every legitimate SAME-ORG write through that FK is
# REFUSED. Fail-closed, but on a target the guard could have read perfectly well.
#
# Invisible to every shipped resource: in samen_core every `postgres do repo … end` is a
# static module, so both calls return the same value and the ORDER cannot be observed. That
# is why the named red builds a destination with a function repo that resolves for `:read`
# only, pointed at the REAL `cpy_company` table, and asserts both halves of the pair before
# exercising the guard.
#
# Flips the named MG-21 red. Its anti-tautology CONTROL — a genuine CROSS-org FK against the
# same destination is still refused with "cross-org FK" — flips too, and that is the point:
# with no repo the guard can neither pass a same-org target nor identify a foreign one, so
# the patch is refutable from both sides. MG-22's red (the one-of-the-pair-missing bail-out)
# stays green: this patch touches ONE line.
#
# One boolean operator. Touches policy/same_org_fk.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/same_org_fk_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-21: a same-org FK PASSES against a target whose repo resolves only for :read
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/policy/same_org_fk.ex
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Policy.SameOrgFk do
   # foreign target from this validation (the whole point is to SEE it and REFUSE it).
   defp target_org_id(rel, fk_value) do
     dest = rel.destination
-    repo = AshPostgres.DataLayer.Info.repo(dest, :read) || AshPostgres.DataLayer.Info.repo(dest)
+    repo = AshPostgres.DataLayer.Info.repo(dest, :read) && AshPostgres.DataLayer.Info.repo(dest)
     table = AshPostgres.DataLayer.Info.table(dest)
 
     dest_pk_source = attribute_source(dest, rel.destination_attribute)
